// d * (1 + 2 * s) / 4 and so need the grid times four: 4,12,20,28,36,44,52,60. The table that ggml-common.h carries (iq3xs_grid,
// copied from vLLM / llama.cpp b2899, ggml's pre-final IQ3_XS grid) has 62 where 15 * 4 = 60, i.e. every grid value 15 was decoded
// as 15.5 (+3.3 %, on 150 of the 2048 table bytes = about 1/8 of all weights). Same indices as iq3xs_grid, only the byte 0x3e became
// 0x3c. ggml-common.h is deliberately left byte-identical (the JIT copy csrc/gguf_iq_mmq/iq_mmq_ggml_common.h is a verbatim prefix of it,
// pinned by test_gguf_iq_mmq_1009.py); iq3xs_grid stays defined there and is no longer referenced by IQ3_S.
// Pinned against gguf-py index for index by test_gguf_iq3s_wheel_1012.py; the same table (name iq3s_grid_ggml) is in
// python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/gguf_iq_mmq/iq_mmq_tiles.cuh since G11.
